    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Start",
      "title": "Whose is it?",
      "learn": [
        "Wessen? The genitive. Masculine and neuter: des plus -(e)s. Feminine and plural: der, and the noun takes no extra -s.",
        "The genitive follows the noun. Das Bett des Patienten. Der Brief des Arztes. Das Auto seines Vaters. Spoken German keeps von: das Bett vom Patienten.",
        "A name takes -s and stands first. Annas Bett. No apostrophe. seines for his plus a masculine or neuter noun. seiner for a feminine noun.",
        "wegen des Fiebers is the written line. wegen is one genitive preposition. The set während, trotz, innerhalb and außerhalb is chapter 77."
      ],
      "minutes": 25,
      "vocab": [
        { "de": "Patient", "article": "der", "plural": "die Patienten", "en": "patient (male)", "emoji": "🏥", "glossaryKey": "patienten" },
        { "de": "Arzt", "article": "der", "plural": "die Ärzte", "en": "doctor (male)", "emoji": "👨‍⚕️", "glossaryKey": "arzt" },
        { "de": "Fieber", "article": "das", "en": "fever", "emoji": "🌡️", "image": { "type": "svg", "id": "thermometer" }, "glossaryKey": "fieber" },
        { "de": "Auto", "article": "das", "plural": "die Autos", "en": "car", "emoji": "🚗", "glossaryKey": "auto" },
        { "de": "Vater", "article": "der", "plural": "die Väter", "en": "father", "emoji": "👨", "glossaryKey": "vaters" }
