      "text": {
        "title": "Das Auto seines Vaters",
        "de": "Das Bett des Patienten ist frei. Der Brief des Arztes liegt hier. Wir warten wegen des Fiebers. Das Auto seines Vaters steht hier. Annas Bett ist frei. Die Tür der Station ist offen.",
        "en": "The patient's bed is free. The doctor's letter is here. We are waiting because of the fever. His father's car is here. Anna's bed is free. The door of the ward is open."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Choose",
      "title": "Wessen?",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "Das Auto seines Vaters",
      "heroImage": "bed",
      "story": [
        "<b>Wessen?</b> Whose? That is the <b>genitive</b>. You already read it in the cases chapter: <b>das Bett des Patienten</b>. On the ward people often say <b>von + dative</b>: <b>das Bett vom Patienten</b>. Both stay correct. The chart uses the genitive.",
        "Masculine and neuter take <b>des</b> and an ending. <b>des Patienten. des Arztes. des Fiebers. seines Vaters.</b> Nouns in <b>-e, -er, -el, -en</b> take only <b>-s</b>: Vater, Fieber. A short noun often takes <b>-es</b>: <b>des Arztes</b>. <b>des Briefes</b> and <b>des Briefs</b> are both correct when Brief itself is genitive. This chart does not choose between them.",
        "Feminine and plural take <b>der</b> and <b>no -s</b> on the noun. <b>Die Tür der Station. Das Bett der Patientin.</b> der is also feminine dative, and nominative masculine: <b>Der Brief</b>. The noun ending shows the job.",
        "<b>Patient</b> adds <b>-en</b> in the genitive: <b>des Patienten</b>. Not des Patient. Not des Patientens. <b>den Patienten</b> and <b>dem Patienten</b> stay the other cases. Herr, Kollege and the full -en table are chapter 64.",
        "A name takes <b>-s</b> and stands <b>before</b> the thing. <b>Annas Bett.</b> No apostrophe. <b>das Bett von Anna</b> stays correct. <b>seines</b> is his plus a masculine or neuter noun: <b>Das Auto seines Vaters. Der Brief seines Arztes.</b> <b>seiner</b> is feminine: <b>Das Bett seiner Patientin.</b>",
        "The genitive <b>follows</b> the noun. <b>Das Auto seines Vaters</b>, not the old order as the model. <b>wegen des Fiebers</b> is because of the fever. <b>des Fiebers wegen</b> is the same words, also correct. The set während, trotz, innerhalb and außerhalb is chapter 77. Everyday wegen plus the dative is heard and is not the written line."
      ],
      "questionRule": "des plus -(e)s for masculine and neuter. der and no -s for feminine and plural. Names take -s and stand first. No apostrophe. seines for his plus masculine or neuter. The genitive follows the noun.",
